From: Shobhit Agarwal <ashobhit@google.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:49:18 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] examples: MiTV-AXSO0 keeps com.android.tv and
 partnercustomizer, which open HDMI and answer the Netflix and Prime buttons

On a Mi TV 4A Pro (MiTV-AXSO0, Android TV 9, PI.6036) another tool had removed both with pm uninstall --user 0:
Settings > Inputs opened nothing and the remote's app buttons were dead. install-existing brought both back.
The key-repeat note gets the set's three rows: InputKeyService cost the volume ramp on Android 9 too, and the
vendor global-key receiver made the helper unnecessary.
---
 docs/devices/tcl-55p71b-g09-key-repeat.md | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 examples/xiaomi-mitv-axso0/debloat.txt    | 11 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+)

diff --git a/docs/devices/tcl-55p71b-g09-key-repeat.md b/docs/devices/tcl-55p71b-g09-key-repeat.md
index d9f39396..f7c14ab4 100644
--- a/docs/devices/tcl-55p71b-g09-key-repeat.md
+++ b/docs/devices/tcl-55p71b-g09-key-repeat.md
@@ -252,6 +252,29 @@ mechanism claimed here is the `capabilities=8` in the dump and the three rows, n
 `KeyboardInterceptor`. The owner kept both buttons and lives with the stepped volume - the second Choice
 below - so nothing in that section changes.
 
+## A Xiaomi Mi TV 4A Pro on Android TV 9, where the app buttons need no helper
+
+Older again: Xiaomi MiTV-AXSO0 (`dangal`, Amlogic), Android TV 9 (SDK 28), firmware `PI.6036`, stock Xiaomi
+Bluetooth remote, launcher built from `main` on 2026-11-02, `com.google.android.tvlauncher` disabled by
+`launcher/build-and-install.sh`. The owner held volume up on the real remote each time:
+
+| `enabled_accessibility_services` | held volume up |
+|---|---|
+| empty (before the helper) | ramps continuously |
+| `com.gathin.tvhome/.InputKeyService` (`dumpsys accessibility`: one service, `capabilities=8`) | one step per press |
+| empty again, `accessibility_enabled 0` | ramps continuously |
+
+So the trade reaches back to Android 9 and to a third SoC vendor. What differs is the way out. The helper had
+been enabled for the Netflix, Prime Video and Mi buttons, which did nothing because an earlier debloat tool had
+removed `com.xiaomi.android.tvsetup.partnercustomizer` with `pm uninstall --user 0`. `dumpsys window policy`
+names that package's `GlobalKeyReceiver` for `KEYCODE_BUTTON_2`, `_3`, `_4`, `_5` and `_15`, and with
+`cmd package install-existing` bringing it back, Netflix (`KEYCODE_BUTTON_3`) and Prime Video
+(`KEYCODE_BUTTON_4`) opened from any app with no helper bound, while volume kept ramping (logcat:
+`GlobalKey: receiving KeyEvent.KEYCODE_BUTTON_3 start netflix`). The Mi button (`KEYCODE_BUTTON_2`) goes to the
+same receiver, which answers `start tvhome`, PatchWall; with PatchWall disabled it does nothing, and the owner
+left it so. On a Xiaomi set whose app buttons went dead, read `dumpsys window policy` for a vendor global-key
+receiver before reaching for a helper: if that package is only disabled or removed, it may be the cheaper fix.
+
 ## A Sony BRAVIA VH21 where the buttons survive the control
 
 The sets above all pay for the ramp with buttons. One does not. Sony BRAVIA XR-55A95K (`BRAVIA_VH21`,
diff --git a/examples/xiaomi-mitv-axso0/debloat.txt b/examples/xiaomi-mitv-axso0/debloat.txt
index 599684c9..0934d7d6 100644
--- a/examples/xiaomi-mitv-axso0/debloat.txt
+++ b/examples/xiaomi-mitv-axso0/debloat.txt
@@ -18,6 +18,17 @@
 #   the launcher installed. Xiaomi's `set_auto_play` setting (1 out of the box) does it:
 #   `settings put global set_auto_play 0` stops it, and the TV then starts on Home.
 #   Undo: `settings put global set_auto_play 1`.
+# - Keep com.android.tv. It is the only app that answers the TV input framework's passthrough URI here
+#   (`pm query-activities -a android.intent.action.VIEW -d content://android.media.tv/passthrough/<input id>
+#   -t vnd.android.cursor.item/channel`), so with it gone Settings > Inputs and the launcher's Inputs menu
+#   open nothing for HDMI 1-3 or AV. A second unit on PI.6036 had lost it to another debloat tool's
+#   `pm uninstall --user 0`; `cmd package install-existing com.android.tv` brought HDMI back.
+# - Keep com.xiaomi.android.tvsetup.partnercustomizer. `dumpsys window policy` lists KEYCODE_BUTTON_2, _3, _4,
+#   _5 and _15 as global keys for its GlobalKeyReceiver: the remote's Netflix button (KEYCODE_BUTTON_3, 190) and
+#   Prime Video button (KEYCODE_BUTTON_4, 191) open those apps from anywhere through it, with no launcher key
+#   helper, so a held volume button keeps ramping. The Mi button (KEYCODE_BUTTON_2, 189) goes there too and
+#   "start tvhome" opens PatchWall: with com.mitv.tvhome.atv off it does nothing, and mapping it with app_keys
+#   and INPUT_KEY_SERVICE=1 cost the volume ramp on that unit (docs/devices/tcl-55p71b-g09-key-repeat.md).
 
